---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="A new era of land transparency · LandControl" description="From 6 April 2027 contractual control agreements over registered land in England and Wales must be reported to HM Land Registry. LandControl turns that data into development intelligence." bodyClass="sub era">
<header class="wrap hero">
  <div class="scan" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <p class="crumb"><a href="/">LandControl</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--red)">The new era</span></p>
    <h1>A new era of land transparency starts in <em>2027.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">Ownership tells you who owns the land. Contractual-control data begins to reveal who controls the opportunity.</p>
    <div class="facts">
      <div><span class="num">6 Apr 2027</span><span>Reporting duty in force</span></div>
      <div><span class="num">Apr 2028</span><span>Public dataset, monthly</span></div>
      <div><span class="num">E &amp; W</span><span>Registered land</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="split">
  <div class="half left wrap">
    <div class="inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">The legislation</p>
      <h2>What changes on 6 April 2027.</h2>
      <p>From 6 April 2027, the Provision of Information (Contractual Control) (Registered Land) Regulations 2026 will require qualifying contractual control agreements over registered land in England and Wales to be reported digitally to HM Land Registry.</p>
      <p>For the first time, information about arrangements such as option agreements, conditional contracts, pre-emption rights and certain promotion agreements will begin entering a structured reporting system.</p>
      <p>Until now, knowing who legally owned a piece of land did not always tell you who actually controlled its development potential. A landowner could still hold the title while a developer had already secured an option or other contractual right over the site.</p>
      <p class="big">The new regime changes that.</p>
      <p>Developers, promoters and other parties will have to provide information including the land affected, the parties involved, the type of agreement and the period of control. Changes such as assignments, variations, exercise and expiry can also trigger further reporting requirements.</p>
      <p>The result is a completely new layer of intelligence entering the UK land market.</p>
      <div class="pair">
        <div><span class="k">Ownership</span><span>tells you who owns the land.</span></div>
        <div><span class="k">Contractual control</span><span>begins to reveal who controls the opportunity.</span></div>
      </div>
      <a class="go" href="/#scope">Read the full scope and the source documents →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="half right wrap">
    <div class="inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">LandControl</p>
      <h2>HM Land Registry will create the data. LandControl makes it commercially useful.</h2>
      <p>Instead of searching separate Land Registry records, planning portals, local plans, company records and mapping systems, LandControl brings development intelligence together in one platform.</p>
      <ul class="does">
        <li>See where developers are securing land.</li>
        <li>Track competitor activity.</li>
        <li>Identify option and contractual-control agreements.</li>
        <li>Monitor important changes and expiry dates.</li>
        <li>Overlay planning applications, land allocations, ownership and development constraints.</li>
        <li>Discover sites that match your acquisition strategy.</li>
        <li>Receive alerts when something important changes.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="qh">LandControl is designed to answer the questions that matter.</p>
      <ol class="qs">
        <li>Who controls this land?</li>
        <li>Which developers are becoming active in this area?</li>
        <li>Which sites may become available?</li>
        <li>Where is development activity moving next?</li>
        <li>Which opportunities should my acquisitions team investigate today?</li>
      </ol>
      <a class="go" href="/#why">See how alerts, discovery and competitor intelligence work →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap band flow">
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="head">
      <p class="eyebrow">From raw land data to development intelligence</p>
      <h2>LandControl continuously monitors the signals that matter and turns them into searchable maps, alerts, site intelligence and opportunity rankings.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="chain">
      <div><span class="k">In</span><strong>HMLR contractual control dataset</strong><span>Monthly. Location, grantee, right, duration, dates.</span></div>
      <div><span class="k">Join</span><strong>Titles · planning · local plans · Companies House · constraints</strong><span>One record per site, grantees resolved to parent groups.</span></div>
      <div><span class="k">Derive</span><strong>Scores, expiries, competitor movement</strong><span>Momentum and opportunity ranking, recalculated on every release.</span></div>
      <div><span class="k">Out</span><strong>Maps · alerts · site intelligence · rankings</strong><span>Delivered to the people and regions you choose.</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="so">So instead of spending hours looking for development opportunities, <strong>LandControl brings the opportunities to you.</strong></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap band close">
  <div class="grid">
    <p class="strap"><span>Find land.</span><span>Track competitors.</span><span>Move first.</span></p>
    <p class="tag">LandControl — Development Intelligence for the New Land Market.</p>
    <div class="ctas"><a class="btn" href="/#briefing">Get the briefing</a><a class="btn alt" href="/#products">See the roadmap and pricing</a></div>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
